# Jobs & console

Match the app's existing job pattern (`ShouldQueue`, connection, queue name). Inspect `config/queue.php` before assuming Redis/Horizon/database.

**Do:** make side-effectful jobs idempotent; keep `$timeout` below `retry_after`; use `ShouldBeUnique` when duplicate dispatches would corrupt state; implement `failed()` when domain state must update after exhaustion.

**Don't:** retry permanent validation failures; dispatch the same non-unique job on every request without a uniqueness key; log payloads that contain secrets.

```php
// Don't — unbounded retries, no uniqueness
class SyncInvoice implements ShouldQueue
{
    public $tries = 0;
}

// Do — bounded backoff + unique per invoice
class SyncInvoice implements ShouldQueue, ShouldBeUnique
{
    public $tries = 4;
    public $backoff = [1, 5, 10];
    public function uniqueId(): string
    {
        return (string) $this->invoice->id;
    }
}
```

If Horizon is not in `composer.json`, do not add it. If it is, follow existing `horizon.php` rather than inventing supervisors.
